  "worked_solution": "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x(vx)^{2}-(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+2(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3})}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+2v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-2{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
